hwlab Espressif USB Serial/JTAG backend (plugins/espusbjtag, internal/riscv)

Implemented independently in Go. No third-party source code is included.

References (specifications and hardware facts, not code):
  * RISC-V Debug Specification 0.13 (public specification): DTM (dtmcs, dmi),
    Debug Module registers, Access Register and System Bus Access semantics.
  * IEEE 1149.1 TAP state machine (public standard).
  * Espressif's published protocol description of the USB Serial/JTAG
    "esp_usb_jtag" bridge (comment block in the OpenOCD driver, GPL-2.0, and
    Espressif documentation): read as DOCUMENTATION of the wire protocol only
    (capability descriptor layout, vendor control requests, nibble command
    encoding). No OpenOCD source was copied, translated or linked, and OpenOCD
    is not run by hwlab. The implementation was then confirmed against, and
    corrected by, a real ESP32-C6.
  * ESP32-C6 register addresses and bit positions (SPI1/SPI_MEM, LP_WDT, timer
    groups, USB Serial/JTAG, eFuse, LP_AON) taken from public ESP-IDF headers
    (Apache-2.0) as documentation; no code was copied. The flash command
    sequence (JEDEC 0x9F, SFDP 0x5A, READ, WREN, PP 0x02, SE 0x20, BE 0xD8,
    CE 0xC7) is the standard SPI-NOR command set (JEDEC JESD216).
  * Observations of a real ESP32-C6 (USB descriptors, IDCODE, DM registers).
  * ESP32-S3 / Xtensa (internal/xtensa, ADR 0038): instruction encodings and
    special-register numbers from Cadence's public Xtensa Instruction Set
    Architecture Reference Manual. OpenOCD's Xtensa and esp32s3 sources
    (GPL-2.0) were read as a REFERENCE ONLY for interface facts (TAP
    instruction codes, OCD register numbers and bits, the LDDR32.P/SDDR32.P/
    RFDO encodings, power-up order); no code was copied, translated or linked.
    ESP32-S3 register addresses, eFuse field positions and flash pins from
    ESP-IDF v5.3 headers and esp_efuse_table.csv (Apache-2.0) and the ESP32-S3
    TRM; esptool (GPL-2.0+) consulted for facts only. Constants were checked on
    a real ESP32-S3 where readable.

internal/usb and internal/jtag are shared with plugins/ftdi.
